 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfA0G4kRj3K/",
 "title": "The Illusion of Wealth Coaches",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator compares fake wealth gurus to people who sell treasure maps instead of finding the treasure themselves. The main lesson is to question the credibility of teachers who sell success formulas without having achieved success themselves.",
 "key_points": [
  "Give a pirate a treasure map, and he spends his whole life looking for the treasure.",
  "A smart man asks why the person selling the maps hasn't found the treasure yet.",
  "Some people teach how to get rich without ever being rich themselves.",
  "They become rich by selling the secrets to become rich.",
  "They never found the treasure; they just got good at selling maps.",
  "Just because someone knows the path doesn't mean they've ever walked it."
 ],
 "content": "Day 147 of sharing #motivationalquotes and #philosophy thoughts everyday… Follow @dragos_andrei_ for more:) Give a pirate a treasure map and he'll spend his whole life looking for the treasure. But give a smart man the same treasure map and he'll ask, why does the man selling the maps hasn't found the treasure yet? That's exactly how some people make a living, they teach you how to get rich without ever being rich themselves. Craziest part, they become rich by selling the secrets to become rich. They never found the treasure. They just got good at selling maps. Just remember, just because someone knows the path doesn't mean they've ever walked it.",
